Z||000000||Monkeyman||04-22-2000||09:59 AM||||Almost 1000 members and I've only logged on the chat once where someone else was there.  Am I missing something or just logging on at the wrong time?  Does everyone know that we have a real time chat room?  (The link is at the bottom of the page, guys! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)  Not that I'm desparate to talk to anyone in particular, but it just seems like it's not as popular as I had thought it might be.  Could it be that everyone else is at work at 8:30am (Indiana time) when I get off (and consequently get on the computer)?  You guys need to become independantly wealthy so you can quit your jobs and talk to me.  (Can you tell that I need a nap?  I feel lazy as I've already taken <B>3</B> this week!)||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||04-22-2000||10:48 AM||||Well, Monkey, I can't get on the chat as I have WebTV. But I figured due to the relative lack of new posts (vs pre-chat days) that EVERYONE was spending all of their time there. Personally, I'm not terribly fond of the chat idea for that reason... <BR> <BR>If there is a different reason for the relative inactivity in the forum (1000 members?! Couldn't tell!) then I am baffled as to the cause.  I'm not really complaining, but since you brought it up, it seems like people really only contribute lately when there is a squabble to join in on.<P>So whaddaya say Monk? Wanna fight?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
